Executives at world football's governing body Fifa on Friday said "incorrect" media reports had "disrupted" the presentation of its proposals to open up the World Cup to outside investors. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b249b2c6-84bd-11f1-b07b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-20T215821Z-755382867-UP1EM7K1P1745-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-WORLDCUP-ESP-CELEBRATIONS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b249b2c6-84bd-11f1-b07b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-20T215821Z-755382867-UP1EM7K1P1745-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-WORLDCUP-ESP-CELEBRATIONS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">af8f94c6-8cbd-11f1-a3f3-51f91fa6bfb9</guid><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 11:46:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b249b2c6-84bd-11f1-b07b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-20T215821Z-755382867-UP1EM7K1P1745-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-WORLDCUP-ESP-CELEBRATIONS.jpg">© Ana Beltran / REUTERS</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>France legend Zidane succeeds Deschamps as boss of Les Bleus</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260728-france-legend-zidane-succeeds-deschamps-as-france-football-coach</link><description>
Zinédine Zidane was officially appointed as France's new head coach on Tuesday, succeeding Didier Deschamps, the French Football Federation announced.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6804e552-8a6f-11f1-a123-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3CZ6DF.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6804e552-8a6f-11f1-a123-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3CZ6DF.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a6222208-8a6c-11f1-b66a-032336fcdb0b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 13:52:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6804e552-8a6f-11f1-a123-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3CZ6DF.jpg">© AFP - Lou Benoist</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Tadej Pogacar wins a record-equaling fifth Tour de France title</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260726-pogacar-wins-record-equalling-fifth-tour-de-france-2</link><description>
Tadej Pogacar claimed his record-equalling fifth Tour de France title as Mathieu van der Poel won a sensational 21st and final stage around Paris on Sunday. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1dbfc5b4-8922-11f1-926e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-26T180350Z-1735657331-UP1EM7Q1DVENF-RTRMADP-3-CYCLING-FRANCE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1dbfc5b4-8922-11f1-926e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-26T180350Z-1735657331-UP1EM7Q1DVENF-RTRMADP-3-CYCLING-FRANCE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">18b2eb86-8914-11f1-92d7-816556919eec</guid><pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 19:06:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1dbfc5b4-8922-11f1-926e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-26T180350Z-1735657331-UP1EM7Q1DVENF-RTRMADP-3-CYCLING-FRANCE.jpg">© Stephanie Lecocq / Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Zizou's back: Zinedine Zidane set to take charge of Les Bleus</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260723-zizou-s-back-zidane-set-to-take-charge-of-les-bleus</link><description>
The French Football Federation will hold a news conference on 28 July to unveil the next coach of the national team, the governing body said on Thursday. Former star player Zinedine Zidane has long been viewed as the leading candidate for the role.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8d86fa42-970c-11eb-8913-005056bff430/w:1024/p:16x9/AP941247635205.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8d86fa42-970c-11eb-8913-005056bff430/w:1024/p:16x9/AP941247635205.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c2658eec-8697-11f1-aec8-517d018704fa</guid><pubDate>Thu, 23 Jul 2026 13:11:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8d86fa42-970c-11eb-8913-005056bff430/w:1024/p:16x9/AP941247635205.jpg">© AP - Francisco Seco </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>France skipper Mbappé denies Messi to win second Golden Boot award</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260720-france-skipper-mbapp%C3%A9-claims-place-in-world-cup-legend-with-second-golden-boot-world-cup-2026</link><description>
Kylian Mbappé will return to France from the World Cup with his reputation as one of the best strikers of his generation enhanced, having become the first player to win the competition's Golden Boot award twice.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/abecbf92-7bdd-11f1-8bd7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/FOOTBALL-FRANCE-MAROC-MBAPPE-BUT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/abecbf92-7bdd-11f1-8bd7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/FOOTBALL-FRANCE-MAROC-MBAPPE-BUT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4affbd34-841f-11f1-ae24-7d8e98d13a62</guid><pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 11:22:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/abecbf92-7bdd-11f1-8bd7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/FOOTBALL-FRANCE-MAROC-MBAPPE-BUT.jpg">IMAGN IMAGES via Reuters - DAVID BUTLER II</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Europe rights body urges Fifa to strengthen integrity of football ahead of 2030</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260720-europe-rights-body-urges-fifa-to-strengthen-integrity-of-football-ahead-of-2030</link><description>
The Council of Europe, a pan-European human rights body, has questioned the integrity of the World Cup and urged governing body Fifa to help build a stronger framework for the 2030 edition being played mostly in Spain and Portugal.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0f53e2ba-840b-11f1-b883-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26200823925312.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0f53e2ba-840b-11f1-b883-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26200823925312.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">04abb85e-8403-11f1-9a16-b35b95c4cc01</guid><pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 07:21:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0f53e2ba-840b-11f1-b883-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26200823925312.jpg">AP Photo/Jacquelyn Martin - Jacquelyn Martin</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Spain's world champions head home to million-strong Madrid welcome</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260720-spain-s-world-champions-head-home-to-million-strong-madrid-welcome</link><description>
Spain's World Cup winners headed home on Monday to a heroes' welcome in Madrid, where a million fans are expected to greet them after a night of raucous celebrations across the country.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3f376688-83fb-11f1-ae08-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/f8ea41e7bcb709b3022a6eebd85d316c4f26a5b8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3f376688-83fb-11f1-ae08-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/f8ea41e7bcb709b3022a6eebd85d316c4f26a5b8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">40193702-83fb-11f1-ade2-fb8869204cb9</guid><pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 05:24:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3f376688-83fb-11f1-ae08-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/f8ea41e7bcb709b3022a6eebd85d316c4f26a5b8.jpg">© Paul Hanna / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Spain crowned world champions as France miss out and England claim bronze</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260720-spain-squeeze-the-life-out-of-argentina-to-take-away-big-new-world-cup-world-cup-2026</link><description>
Spain compressed Argentina to claim the first 48-team World Cup and conclude a 39-day extravaganza of 104 matches, 308 goals at 16 stadiums in the United States, Mexico and Canada.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7c96edda-83da-11f1-a475-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-19T230635Z-570261947-UP1EM7J1S6XKE-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-WORLDCUP-ESP-ARG.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7c96edda-83da-11f1-a475-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-19T230635Z-570261947-UP1EM7J1S6XKE-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-WORLDCUP-ESP-ARG.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">142c4782-8375-11f1-8122-bba2e6621155</guid><pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 03:48:59 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7c96edda-83da-11f1-a475-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-19T230635Z-570261947-UP1EM7J1S6XKE-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-WORLDCUP-ESP-ARG.jpg">© Kai Pfaffenbach / Reuters</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Torres' extra-time strike seals Spain's second World Cup as Argentina finish with 10 men</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260719-spain-outwit-argentina-to-claim-2026-world-cup-world-cup-2026</link><description>
Substitute Ferran Torres struck 37 seconds into the second period of extra-time to edge Spain past a 10-man Argentina and give his side a second World Cup trophy.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dd151b58-83c3-11f1-bf2a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-19T224620Z-1742739363-UP1EM7J1R96DZ-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-WORLDCUP-ESP-ARG.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dd151b58-83c3-11f1-bf2a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-19T224620Z-1742739363-UP1EM7J1R96DZ-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-WORLDCUP-ESP-ARG.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f31896a8-83b6-11f1-8f45-0fa873d88c2f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 19 Jul 2026 23:18:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dd151b58-83c3-11f1-bf2a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-19T224620Z-1742739363-UP1EM7J1R96DZ-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-WORLDCUP-ESP-ARG.jpg">REUTERS - Kai Pfaffenbach</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Spain face Argentina in battle for World Cup supremacy</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260719-spain-face-argentina-in-battle-for-world-cup-supremacy-world-cup-2026</link><description>
Defending champions Argentina take on reigning European champions Spain on Sunday afternoon in a World Cup final shimmering with subplots and story lines.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/92ed4e3c-5057-11f1-91d6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-14T222008Z-1594628161-RC299LA8HJND-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-WORLDCUP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/92ed4e3c-5057-11f1-91d6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-14T222008Z-1594628161-RC299LA8HJND-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-WORLDCUP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7d008caa-82da-11f1-8024-13193228ceb9</guid><pubDate>Sun, 19 Jul 2026 12:26:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/92ed4e3c-5057-11f1-91d6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-14T222008Z-1594628161-RC299LA8HJND-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-WORLDCUP.jpg">REUTERS - Eduardo Munoz</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Saka hits three as England beat France in 10-goal thriller for third place</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260718-saka-hits-three-as-england-beat-france-in-10-goal-thriller-for-third-place</link><description>
Bukayo Saka hit a hat trick as England edged past France 6-4 on Saturday afternoon to claim a zany bronze medal match in Miami.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/695e2996-82fd-11f1-8b47-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/saka.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/695e2996-82fd-11f1-8b47-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/saka.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c6b46ef0-82ff-11f1-adce-1fed46e2a2b5</guid><pubDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 23:29:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/695e2996-82fd-11f1-8b47-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/saka.jpg">Getty Images via AFP - LUKE HALES</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Pogacar wins 'unforgettable' Tour de France 14th stage to extend overall lead</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260718-pogacar-wins-unforgettable-tour-de-france-14th-stage-to-extend-overall-lead</link><description>
Tadej Pogacar won an "unforgettable" mountainous 14th stage of the Tour de France amidst huge crowds in the Vosges on Saturday to extend his lead over Jonas Vingegaard to four and a half minutes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e979a49e-82c0-11f1-82f7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/c6ca17b54c5dc358f612844c6f601d29acf1a2ce.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e979a49e-82c0-11f1-82f7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/c6ca17b54c5dc358f612844c6f601d29acf1a2ce.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6ebe283a-82c3-11f1-892a-792519af272c</guid><pubDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 16:12:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e979a49e-82c0-11f1-82f7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/c6ca17b54c5dc358f612844c6f601d29acf1a2ce.jpg">© Anne-Christine POUJOULAT / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>France and England bosses say squads will take World Cup play off seriously</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260718-france-and-england-bosses-say-squads-will-take-world-cup-play-off-seriously</link><description>
France head coach Didier Deschamps and his England counterpart Thomas Tuchel say their teams will play Saturday's World Cup third place play-off game with intensity despite the disappointment of losing their semi-finals against Spain and Argentina respectively.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a3764ea4-826e-11f1-86ce-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/desss-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a3764ea4-826e-11f1-86ce-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/desss-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dac582e0-823b-11f1-ad48-0b87ea9fc21b</guid><pubDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 06:16:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a3764ea4-826e-11f1-86ce-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/desss-1.jpg">AFP - CHANDAN KHANNA</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Argentina see off England to reach World Cup showdown with Spain</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260715-argentina-see-off-england-to-reach-world-cup-final-showdown-with-spain</link><description>
Argentina scored two late goals on Wednesday to eliminate England 2-1 and advance to the 2026 World Cup final against Spain on Sunday. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/31be05f6-80a5-11f1-bef7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/laut.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/31be05f6-80a5-11f1-bef7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/laut.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5b669ae0-80a4-11f1-869e-45cc9bf0894e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 15 Jul 2026 23:44:06 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/31be05f6-80a5-11f1-bef7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/laut.jpg">Getty Images via AFP - SHAUN BOTTERILL</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Sixty years after rivalry took root, England and Argentina duel for place in final</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260715-sixty-years-after-rivalry-took-root-england-and-argentina-duel-for-place-in-final</link><description>
The rivalry between England and Argentina is firmly rooted in the 1966 World Cup. Sixty years later, the two meet to compete for a place in the final against Spain on Sunday. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c5b4984e-7ebe-11f1-9dd8-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Design-sans-titre-6-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c5b4984e-7ebe-11f1-9dd8-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Design-sans-titre-6-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8c0b73ce-7fb3-11f1-824b-a3dc39ed0e73</guid><pubDate>Wed, 15 Jul 2026 14:49:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c5b4984e-7ebe-11f1-9dd8-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Design-sans-titre-6-2.jpg">© AP</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>French fans come to terms with World Cup exit after Spain defeat</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260715-french-fans-come-to-terms-with-world-cup-exit-after-spain-defeat</link><description>
French supporters who had travelled to Dallas for the semi-final against Spain left the stadium disappointed, but admitting grudging respect for a well-organised opponent. There was little appetite for excuses and gratitude towards Didier Deschamps – as well as curiosity over what's to come when France legend Zinedine Zidane steps into his shoes. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c676b6b0-8038-11f1-8380-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/shared-image.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c676b6b0-8038-11f1-8380-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/shared-image.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f2dd419a-803f-11f1-9591-97b854f17fd5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 15 Jul 2026 12:20:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c676b6b0-8038-11f1-8380-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/shared-image.jpg">© RFI/Zeenat Hansrod</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>2026 World Cup venues: Atlanta</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260715-2026-world-cup-venues-atlanta-world-cup-2026</link><description>
Sixteen stadiums in Mexico, Canada and the United States have staged the games during the first 48-team World Cup. RFI looks at Atlanta Stadium which will host the semi-final between England and Argentina.
